ull, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "David Bowie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "classic rock": {"genre": "classic rock", "country_code": "sk", "country_name": "Slovakia", "summary": "Classic rock was originally conceived as a radio station programming format which evolved from the album oriented rock (AOR) format in the early-1980s. In the United States, this rock music format now features a large playlist of songs ranging from the 1960s, 1970s, 1980s and early 1990s, with some stations including a limited number of current releases.\n\nThe classic rock stations recreate the sound of Album Oriented Rock (AOR) stations of the 60s-90s (although usually with a much more limited playlist) and appeal mainly to adults.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "David Bowie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Fleetwood Mac", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Pink Floyd", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Queen", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Beatles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "dance-pop": {"genre": "dance-pop", "country_code": "sk", "country_name": "Slovakia", "summary": "Dance-pop is a style of electronic dance music and a subgenre of pop music that evolved from Disco, circa 1981, that combines dance beats with a pop/R'n'B song structure. Because there is such an emphasis on fully-formed songs in dance-pop, it's often viewed as a separate classification unto itself apart from pure dance. Dance-pop is also closely related to the teen pop and Eurodance movements in the mid-1980s and late 1990s, the rise of boy bands and girl groups, and the reintroduction of the vocoder and similar such innovations.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": 57905, "best_position": 3}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": 11518, "best_position": 52}, {"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": 10629, "bes